  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MCQQuestionData
  questionText: 4. When during the approach should the reported aerodrome altimeter
    setting be set?
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: During descent, the pilot changes from standard pressure setting
    to the reported aerodrome QNH when passing the transition level, allowing altitude
    to be correctly referenced to mean sea level.
  options:
  - When passing 3000 ft AMSL or 1000 ft AGL
  - When passing the transition level
  - When passing the transition altitude
  - Within the transition layer
  correctOptionIndex: 1
